<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dialogue of a Man and His Ba</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dispute between a Man and His Ba</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dialogue of a Man and His Ba is an Egyptian literary text of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-francia">Middle Kingdom</a>, preserved on a single <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papyrus">papyrus</a> now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>. In it a man weary of life argues with his ba, his soul, about death and suicide, in a mixture of prose and poems. It is one of the earliest reflective works on the meaning of life and death.</p></div>
